A dialog that demands a response - for destructive or high-stakes confirmations.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/alert-dialog)

<%= embed UI::AlertDialogPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
AlertDialog do
  AlertDialogTrigger { |trigger| Button(**trigger, variant: :destructive) { "Delete project" } }
  AlertDialogContent do
    AlertDialogHeader do
      AlertDialogTitle { "Delete this project?" }
      AlertDialogDescription { "This can't be undone." }
    end
    AlertDialogFooter do
      AlertDialogClose { |close| Button(**close, variant: :outline) { "Cancel" } }
      button_to "Delete", project_path(@project), method: :delete, class: …
    end
  end
end
```

[Dialog](<%= page_path(:dialog) %>)'s parts under `AlertDialog*` names, with `role="alertdialog"`, a narrower card,
no corner close button and no dismissal by clicking outside - the user has to pick an action (Escape still cancels).
Put the cancel action first and give the confirm button the destructive variant.

